// REQUIRES: host-linux-amd64 || host-linux-arm64
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/run-golden.py --src %S/Inputs/own/units-glue.gopp %S/Inputs/own/units-glue.out
// RUN: %gopp build -emit=gir %S/Inputs/own/units-glue.gopp -o - | FileCheck %s
// GOLDEN: by-hand
// P04.09 review R17: types that differ only in their units are one GIR type,
// and their glue is shared only when it calls no method the program wrote
// (Lowering::glueKey, reachesUserGlue): `Dropped[M]` and `Dropped[KM]` each
// have a drop glue that calls their own `drop`, and the clone glue of a
// slice of `Cloned[KM]` calls `Cloned[KM]`'s Clone, each with its own units.
// (run/own-units.test is the other side: no such method, one glue.)
// CHECK-COUNT-2: fn _GPTdIN4mainE7Dropped
// CHECK-NOT: fn _GPTdIN4mainE7Dropped
